WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
A big part of language learning is
starting to notice the patterns of the

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:08.189
language. Every time you pay a little
attention to a word or a phrase that you

00:00:08.189 --> 00:00:12.719
have saved, a LingQ, let's say, that you
move the status up from two to three,

00:00:12.719 --> 00:00:17.310
which you can do manually. Let's say that
you create a tag ,let's say that you

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:21.840
review your LingQs of the day, which are
sent to you according to a a spaced

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:26.430
repetition system, in other words
designed to help you remember them

00:00:26.430 --> 00:00:31.890
before you completely forget them. All of
these things help you notice, and you

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:36.090
should pay attention when you see
certain phrases, maybe phrases that you

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:41.460
have saved and tagged if you hear them
again, try to pay a little attention to

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:45.320
it. The more you deliberately try to
notice things, whether it be

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:50.730
pronunciation, structure, relationship
between words that might have similar

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:56.640
meanings, all of this effort to notice is
gonna help your brain eventually keep

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:04.340
these things in your long-term memory. So
make an effort to notice.

